chapter-29.md:227: "He's standing out there with everything he owns. I had it not a minute ago. And I can't so much as feel that he's alive, except that he's warm." She looked down at her two broad palms, as she had looked at them in a hollow of shale, and this time there was no puzzlement in her face. "They told me, and I never checked. Thirty rounds."
chapter-29.md:273: Then he did the second thing. He had not been sure, a minute ago, that he would.
